    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23871" root="صخد" body-key="S">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَيْخَدٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَخَدَانٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الصَّيْخَدُ</span>, (L, K,)
or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَيْخَدُ الشَّمْسِ</span>, (A,) <i>The rays</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيْن</span>) <i>of the
sun:</i> (A, L, K:) so called because of the heat
thereof. (L.) One says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَابَ صَيْخَدُ الشَّمْسِ</span>
[<i>The rays of the sun became intensely hot</i>], (A,)
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَذَابَ الصَّيْخَدُ</span> [which means the same].
(L.)

